THOUGHT 1: The detection call failed due to a runtime/service error. I'll wrap the detection call in a try/except to catch that failure and, if detection yields no boxes or raises an exception, fall back to sliding_window_detection to search for the measuring cup. The code will safely handle None/exception returns, display any annotated outputs, and zoom into the first found box (from either method) so we can read the cup markings.

ACTION 1:
